    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d699">

                <pb facs="0762" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002 Manchuria/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain (Atherton) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-02T12:00:00+00:00">April 2,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 2—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. In view of British Government’s opinion expressed in my telegram 126, April
                    1, 5 p.m., I shall take no action on Department’s 105, April 1, 4 p.m., without
                    further instructions.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d699-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d699-f1" n="38" xml:id="d699-f1-content">
                <p>The Department replied in telegram No. 107, April 3, 2 p.m.: “Withhold action
                    until further instructed.” (693.002 Manchuria/39)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
